From d48a2f2712283ec3d2ccfcf88445b170f95dbd83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Mar 2026 04:27:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/12] rw-system.sh: defensive guards, securize rework, and build
 fixes

Combine several rw-system.sh and base.mk changes into a single patch:

Defensive guards for vndk detection failures:
Guard all vndk numeric comparisons with [ -n "$vndk" ] to prevent
shell arithmetic errors when vndk-detect fails. Guard first_api_level
assignment. Change color management setprop to resetprop_phh -n for
fallback-only behaviour. Guard focaltech sysfs search with driver
presence check.

Drop ro.control_privapp_permissions downgrade:
GrapheneOS ships ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce for security.
Remove the unconditional override to 'log' that silently downgrades
enforcement.

VNDK v30 support:
Add VNDK v30 to PRODUCT_EXTRA_VNDK_VERSIONS in base.mk so devices
shipping with VNDK 30 vendor images find matching libraries at runtime.

Securize rework:
Move security-sensitive prop spoofing to post-boot in phh-on-boot.sh.
Add GSI fingerprint change detection (persisted to /metadata) to
signal PMS for post-upgrade steps via persist.pm.mock-upgrade. Expand
device/brand/model/manufacturer property copying from vendor to system.
Add USB gadget string updates. Add persist.sys.phh.securize toggle.
Remove stale ro.adb.secure=0 entries from base.mk and system.prop.

Co-authored-by: Alberto Ponces <ponces26@gmail.com>
